# spike 03 bench, release build

## Stack used per call that isn't a tail call

- command, then more: 2001 calls deep used 2469 KiB, 1264 bytes a call
- inside an expression: 2001 calls deep used 6909 KiB, 3537 bytes a call
- fib-style, two calls: 2001 calls deep used 6909 KiB, 3537 bytes a call
- inside REPEAT and IFELSE lists: 2001 calls deep used 9313 KiB, 4768 bytes a call

Worst case 4768 bytes a call, so a 256 MiB stack fits about 56244 calls.
Endless recursion through lists, no depth limit: stopped by the stack guard at 56246 calls: "DOWN called itself too many times: 56246 calls deep. Does it have a way to STOP?"

